 Let $x = a - b$ and $y = ab.$ We have $a = \dfrac{y}{b}.$ As $a > b > 0,$ $y > 0$ and $b \in \left(0,\sqrt{y}\right).$ Further,
\begin{align*}
a + \frac{1}{b(a - b)}
&= \frac{y}{b} + \frac{1}{b x} \\
&= \frac{yx + 1}{by} \\
&= \frac{yx + 1}{b\left(a - b\right)} \\
&= \frac{yx + 1}{y\left(\dfrac{y}{b} - b\right)} \\
&= \frac{yx + 1}{y\left(\frac{y}{b} - b\right)} \\
&= \frac{y^2 + \frac{1}{y}}{y^2 - \left(\dfrac{y}{b}\right)b}
\end{align*}
It follows that $m = y^2 - \left(\dfrac{y}{b}\right)b \le y^2$ and
\[y^2 - m = \left(\dfrac{y}{b}\right)b \ge y\]
So, by AM-GM,
\[y^2 + \frac{1}{y} = m + y + \left(y^2 - m\right) \ge 3\sqrt[3]{y\left(y^2 - m\right)} = 3\sqrt[3]{y\left(\dfrac{y}{b}\right)b} = 3\sqrt[3]{y^3} = 3y.\] Since $y > 0,$ we have $y^2 + \frac{1}{y} \ge 3y.$ and further,
\[a + \frac{1}{b(a - b)}
= \frac{y^2 + \frac{1}{y}}{y^2 - \left(\frac{y}{b}\right)b}
\ge \frac{3y}{y^2}
= \frac{3}{y}
= \frac{3ab}{ab^2} = \frac{3ab}{ab - b^2}.\] Note that $b \in \left(0,\sqrt{y}\right).$ If $b \to \sqrt{y},$ $ab \to y$ and $ab - b^2 \to b(a - b) = x.$ Thus, the expression $a + \frac{1}{b(a - b)}$ approaches $\frac{3}{x}.$ It follows that the minimum value of $a + \frac{1}{b(a - b)}$ is $\boxed{\frac{3}{x}}.$</think> <answer> $\dfrac{3}{x}$ </answer>

